ins  to you know within two years we had 10  000 square feet of space i had 40  employees and you know working just  underneath me alone half of them had  criminal backgrounds but they were  incredible people but being five foot  one i had to every day basically show up  to be like you're gonna let these people  push you around are you gonna you know  be able to lead and that continuous  facing myself every day not knowing my s  not having skills learning every day  saying okay lisa you can go into this  not knowing it and learn or you can say  yeah this is too scary but if i don't do  it i lose my house because our house was  up for collateral  so  yeah but in that process right it didn't  give me the luxury of saying well i  don't know how to run a team i don't  even know how to you know um to build a  a warehouse i didn't give myself the  luxury and every time i didn't give  myself the luxury  and i found had an obstacle that i then  figured out  it gave me that like  validation within myself that for so  many years i was searching for outside  of myself i was searching for my husband  to come home every day and validate me  because i made nice dinner right i was  waiting for validation for my parents to  tell me i was a good wife i was waiting  for validation from so many extra  external people or things  that having that pivot putting myself in  these situations where i didn't think i  was capable and then going oh my god i'm  actually capable to figure it out  gave me that idea of what else am i  capable of  and that was the thing of i don't know  what i'm capable of i don't know where  i'm going but the idea that who i am  today does not dictate who i can be  tomorrow was so intoxicating  that i was like i need to do more of  this and that's where i started to pivot  and say what life do i actually want and  by golly i'm gonna freaking demand it of  myself  yeah you and tom are such like  go-getters you guys are crazy  um because i know he has so much of this